# Template License

This repository is currently a template and does not enforce a specific license yet.

When creating a new project from this template, choose a license that fits your project's goals.

---

## Choosing a License

You can explore open-source licenses and find the right one for your project here:

- [Choose an Open Source License (choosealicense.com)](https://choosealicense.com/)
- [Open Source Initiative (OSI) Licenses](https://opensource.org/licenses)

### Common Options:

- **MIT License**: Simple and permissive; allows others to do anything with your code as long as they provide attribution and don't hold you liable.
- **Apache 2.0**: Permissive license that also provides an express grant of patent rights from contributors to users.
- **GNU GPLv3**: Copyleft license requiring derivative works to remain open source under the same terms.
- **Unlicense / CC0**: Dedicates your work to the public domain.

Replace the contents of this file with your chosen license text.
